    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan converges on a Hold with clear tactical guidance. The bull case is technically sound \u2014 JPM trades above the 10-day EMA ($189.34), 50-day SMA ($187.33), and rising 200-day SMA ($164.93), with a fresh bullish MACD crossover and RSI at 59.5. However, the bear's entry-point concerns are decisive: price sits just $1.32 below the upper Bollinger Band ($194.35) and $2.42 below the May 17 high ($195.45) that already rejected price once, and the close $0.33 off the high on the heaviest volume of the month signals distribution. Critically, there is no earnings, sentiment, news, or macro confirmation available, and negative operating cash flow (-$154.2B) and net cash outflow (-$56.4B) cut against the growth narrative. The risk/reward at $193 is balanced, so I maintain the position without chasing, awaiting either a pullback to the $187-189 support cluster or a confirmed breakout above $195.45.\n\n**Entry Price**: 188.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 182.79\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral-to-slightly-underweight allocation; no leverage\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
